For some reason this reminds me of the Coke&#x2F;New Coke fiasco, which ended up popularizing Coke Classic more than ever before.<p>&gt; Consumers were outraged and demanded their beloved Coke back – the taste that they knew and had grown up with. The request to bring the old product back was so loud that soon journalists suggested that the entire project was a stunt. To this accusation Coca-Cola President Don Keough replied on July 10, 1985:<p><pre><code>    &quot;We are not that dumb, and we are not that smart.&quot;
</code></pre>
